      "writtenOn": "2016-11-27T16:54:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The LED light behavior is opposite to brightness.\n\nWhat does that mean? Isn\u0027t the higher the PWM duty cycle the brighter it will be? But it sounds like the input to pwm_set_duty() is the opposite? Lower numbers mean more duty?\n\nThere\u0027s a really funky thing going on in pwm_set_raw_duty() of something being active low vs active high which does some inversion.\n\nThese abstractions need to be cleaned up and if we need to work around the assumptions in npcx then we should add a wrapper in this module with comments documenting the unexpected behavior. Putting inversions within this code just makes everything very hard to understand.",
